# skillforge telemetry — the CANONICAL profile-A (compliance) reference config.
#
# Sources: concept + the PUBLIC Claude Code / OpenTelemetry env-var names; zero third-party
# skills-factory files (clean-room). Realizes docs/10-telemetry-and-grafana.md §"Turning it on"
# under the residency/ZDR posture of docs/14-deployment-profiles.md §"Profile A".
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (T-HARD-10(a)). docs/10/11 require telemetry to stay secret-free AND
# content-free under profile A, but the rule had no enforcement. This is the SHIPPED safe example,
# and it is LINTED in CI by `tools/telemetry-config-lint.js` (src/core/telemetry-config.js):
#   - NO prompt/tool-input content logging under profile A (the switches stay OFF / absent), and
#   - the OTLP auth header is a secret REFERENCE (a ${PLACEHOLDER} the backend resolves), NEVER an
#     inline token (docs/11 references-not-values).
# So the example the operator copies is proven profile-A-safe, not merely asserted to be.
#
# This is a REFERENCE (data), not a value: there is no real secret here — the bearer token is a
# placeholder resolved by the deployment's secret backend at run time.

# 1. Master switch (opt-in — off by default).
CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1

# 2. What to export.
OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp
OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp

# 3. Where to send it.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://collector:4317

# 4. Auth — a secret REFERENCE, never an inline token. ${OTLP_BEARER_TOKEN} is resolved by the
#    deployment's secret backend (env / .env / keychain / Vault / cloud secret manager — docs/11
#    §"Secret backends"). Rotating the token is a backend operation; this reference never changes.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer ${OTLP_BEARER_TOKEN}

# 5. Prompt / tool-input CONTENT logging — DELIBERATELY OFF under profile A. Enabling either would
#    route CLIENT CONTENT into the telemetry plane and void the EU-residency/ZDR promise. Left at
#    their secure defaults (absent = off); shown here only to document the posture.
# OTEL_LOG_USER_PROMPTS=0   # must NOT be enabled under profile A
# OTEL_LOG_TOOL_INPUTS=0    # must NOT be enabled under profile A
